# Jira comment format (Cloud - proven)

Novopay Jira is **Cloud**. Comments paste as **Markdown**, not Server wiki. Proven 2026-08-18 on HDP-8926 (agent-side API pack).

**Always share Jira comment drafts in this format.** Do not use wiki (`h3.`, `||col||`, `[HDP-1|url]`, `{code}`, `{panel}`).

## Paste

1. Draft in Markdown (file or chat).
2. User pastes into comment **Markup** (`Ctrl+Shift+D` or Insert -> Markup), not Visual with wiki.
3. Tables render **after Save**, not in the editor.

Do not post to Jira unless the user explicitly asks.

## Working syntax

- Headings: `##` / `###` / `####` (never `h3.`)
- Bold: `**text**` (never `*text*` wiki)
- Lists: `- item`
- Horizontal rule: `---`
- Tables: GitHub markdown. Header row, then `| --- | --- |`, then data rows. **Max 5 columns** - split wider tables (A / B) so Cloud comments render.
- ASCII hyphen-minus only (` - `, not em/en dash)
- No `{code}`, `{panel}`, `{info}`, or `{apiName}` (curly macros break the comment)
- No JSON / fenced code if the user does not want a code block look; use field tables instead

## S.No. vs tickets (do not mix)

| Column | Format | Why |
|---|---|---|
| S.No. | backticks only: `` `1` `` | Plain number gets smart-linked; wiki `(1)` becomes an emoticon |
| Ticket IDs | `[HDP-8961](https://novopay.atlassian.net/browse/HDP-8961)` | Only in Through-ticket / related-ticket cells or prose |
| Plain `HDP-8961` in a table with markdown links nearby | Do not | Cloud mis-attaches the link to S.No. |

Never put a markdown/wiki link on the S.No. cell. Never leave tickets as unlinked keys when the user asked for hyperlinks.

